# VideoResearcher Workflow

- This repository is an Agent-operable Git project for local video understanding, not a standalone end-user app.
- `scripts/process_video.py` owns deterministic processing only: input validation, audio extraction, transcription, draft index generation, draft note generation, and logs.
- Script-generated notes are drafts. Treat `notes/video_note.draft.md` as an input for Agent synthesis, not as the final user-readable note.
- The final `notes/video_note.md` must be produced or updated by an Agent synthesis pass that reads `transcript/`, `index/`, and draft notes.
- Do not overwrite a human/Agent-authored `notes/video_note.md` by rerunning Phase 3 scripts.
- A final note must include substantive conclusions, evidence time ranges, why each point matters, follow-up questions, and quality boundaries.
- For `B_overview` transcripts, write conclusions as analysis drafts with explicit uncertainty; do not present low-confidence details as final facts.
